    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d67">

                <pb facs="0111" n="101" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg101"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 E.W./5–1245: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hurley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-12T09:00:00+07:00">May 12, 1945—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>773. As the Department will note (my telegram 772, May 12<anchor n="37"
                        xml:id="d67-f1"/>), the Generalissimo in his V–E<anchor n="38"
                        xml:id="d67-f2"/> Day address delivered at a reception attended by the
                    Diplomatic Corps and highest officials of the National Government stressed: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Tribute to U. S. S. R., Britain and United States for victory in the
                            West,</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Tribute to President Roosevelt and</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Rededication of Chinese Government and people to the task of defeating
                            Japan.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>This address was extremely well received and should have excellent effect.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hurley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d67-f1" n="37" xml:id="d67-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d67-f2" n="38" xml:id="d67-f2-content">
                <p>Victory—Europe, May 8, when German armies surrendered.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
